# A REPEATED OPERAND IN AN N-ARY DISJOINTNESS. OWL 2 makes AllDisjointClasses
# members pairwise disjoint BY POSITION, so (A B A) makes A disjoint from
# itself: A is UNSATISFIABLE. The OWL API stores the members as a set and drops
# the repeat silently, so HermiT and ELK behind it answer "A satisfiable" —
# the harness therefore does not diff this fixture against either oracle
# (census.repeated_operands). HOWL must still get it right. Found through ELK's
# conformance test DisjointSelf (corpus/conformance.py).
# Expect: INCOHERENT, A unsatisfiable, B satisfiable, exit 1.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class .
[] a owl:AllDisjointClasses ; owl:members ( :A :B :A ) .
